  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `crates/app/src/geometry/import/native.rs` is new. It holds the shared qualified-extension table. The table is empty. Each native CAD extension that is not in the table is refused by name. This includes IGES and `.prt`.\n- `crates/app/src/geometry/import/cadmpeg/` is new. It runs the external `cadmpeg` program and gives the STEP text to the STEP importer.\n  - It uses the stated path first. If no path is stated, it searches `PATH`.\n  - It requires version `0.6.12` or newer.\n  - It runs `cadmpeg check --json <input>`.\n  - It runs `cadmpeg convert <input> -o <out> --to step --reject-lossy=export`. It never gives `--allow-errors`.\n  - The file path is one argument of the child process. No shell runs.\n  - Each run uses a private folder below the temp folder. A `Drop` guard removes the folder.\n  - A time limit stops the child. A 16 MiB limit applies to the output that the child prints. `MAX_FILE_BYTES` applies to the STEP file.\n- `ImportModel::checked_budget` uses the table. The hardcoded `\"iges\" | \"igs\"` arm is removed.\n- `ViewPrefs` has the new optional field `cadmpeg_path` (`cadmpegPath` in `camcraft-prefs/1`). The key is written only when it is set. Older files load unchanged.\n- The UI keeps a stated `cadmpegPath` when it saves the preferences. No UI control sets the path. That is the work of #1876.\n- The module `cadmpeg` is compiled only when the target is not `wasm32`.\n\nNo shipped import reaches the runner now, because the table is empty. #1875 adds the formats.\n\n## Cause\n\nThis is new work for #1572. It is not a defect fix.\n\n## Deviation from the issue\n\nThe issue asks for a `cadmpeg formats --json` probe. cadmpeg 0.6.12 does not have this option. `formats` prints a text table only. The first worker on this issue reported this.\n\nThis PR does not parse that table. The exit status of `check` and of `convert` is the capability test. A build that cannot read the format or cannot write STEP fails one of the two commands, and the import is refused with the last error line of cadmpeg. `docs/decisions/1873-cadmpeg-runner.md` records this decision and four others. The maintainer can reject it.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew suite `crates/app/tests/cadmpeg_import.rs` (13 tests). It uses the stand-in program `testdata/stubs/cadmpeg_stub.sh`. The stub tests are `#[cfg(unix)]`.\n\n- `unqualified_native_extensions_are_refused_by_name`\n- `a_qualified_extension_routes_to_the_converter`\n- `stub::a_converted_part_imports_through_the_step_importer`\n- `stub::the_program_is_found_on_the_search_path_when_no_path_is_set`\n- `stub::a_missing_program_is_refused_naming_cadmpeg_and_the_extension`\n- `stub::an_old_version_is_refused_by_number`\n- `stub::a_failed_check_is_refused_and_nothing_is_converted`\n- `stub::a_blocking_finding_is_refused_even_with_exit_status_zero`\n- `stub::a_hung_program_is_stopped_at_the_time_limit_and_its_folder_removed`\n- `stub::a_failed_or_empty_conversion_is_refused`\n- `stub::an_oversized_step_is_refused`\n- `stub::output_past_the_capture_limit_stops_the_program`\n- `stub::garbage_output_is_refused_by_the_step_importer`\n\nOther pins:\n\n- `view_prefs`: `cadmpeg_path_survives_a_restart_and_old_preferences_still_load`. The test `offline_only_survives_and_the_file_stores_zero_keys` has the new key in its key list.\n- `camcraft-ui` lib: `prefs_door::a_pick_keeps_the_stated_cadmpeg_path`.\n\nRed before the change: the pins did not compile on `upstream/main` (`import::native`, `import::cadmpeg` and `ViewPrefs::cadmpeg_path` did not exist).\n\nMutation results. Each guard was removed, the pin was red, the guard was restored, the pin was green.\n\n| Guard removed | Red test |\n|---|---|\n| `from_json` reads `cadmpegPath` | `cadmpeg_path_survives_...`, `offline_only_survives_...` |\n| blank path filter in `from_json` | `cadmpeg_path_survives_...` |\n| unqualified refusal in `checked_budget` | `unqualified_native_extensions_are_refused_by_name` |\n| stated path must be a program file | `a_missing_program_is_refused_...` |\n| minimum version | `an_old_version_is_refused_by_number` |\n| `check` exit status | `a_failed_check_is_refused_...` |\n| blocking findings count | `a_blocking_finding_is_refused_...` |\n| report that is not JSON | `a_blocking_finding_is_refused_...` |\n| time limit | `a_hung_program_is_stopped_...` |\n| stop of the child at a limit | `a_hung_program_is_stopped_...` (process id check) |\n| capture limit | the capture-limit test |\n| STEP size limit (loop and final check) | `an_oversized_step_is_refused` |\n| `convert` exit status | `a_failed_or_empty_conversion_is_refused` |\n| empty output | `a_failed_or_empty_conversion_is_refused` |\n| folder removal in `Drop` | 9 stub tests (folder count) |\n| UI save keeps the path | `a_pick_keeps_the_stated_cadmpeg_path` |\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` is green: 44 steps, 0 failed. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. `git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No real cadmpeg ran. It is not installed here. The command line comes from the public help text and README of cadmpeg 0.6.12.\n- No real `check --json` report was read. The runner trusts the exit status and also scans each `findings` list for severity `error` or `blocking`.\n- Windows and macOS did not run. The stub tests are Unix only.\n- The `wasm32` build did not run. The target is not installed here.\n- The path from `ImportModel::within` to the runner is not reached while the table is empty. The tests call `cadmpeg::load_open_within` and `native::route_in` directly.\n- Only the direct child is stopped at a limit. A grandchild process is not stopped (decision 3).\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNo open PR changes the same function.\n\n- #2664 adds one line to the module list of `crates/app/src/geometry/import/mod.rs`. It touches the same file, different lines; whichever merges second refreshes.\n- #2665 appends code to the end of `crates/app/src/prefs.rs`. It touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\n\n## Notes\n\n- The MCP tool and the script verb do not change. #1877 owns them. This PR adds no command.\n- The stub is committed with mode `100755`. The tests link to it, so no test writes a program file.\n\nChangelog: An import can convert a native CAD file to STEP through the optional `cadmpeg` program (version check, private temp folder, time and size limits); no format is enabled yet, and each native extension is refused by name.\n\nEffort: max\n\nFixes #1873\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
